.TH LIBRDP-COCOA-SERVER 1 "2026-07-19" "librdp 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
librdp-cocoa-server \- expose a macOS display or window through librdp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B librdp-cocoa-server
.B --allow-capture
.B --tls-cert
.I path
.B --tls-key
.I path
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B librdp-cocoa-server
shares a display or window from the active macOS graphical session. Capture,
input, clipboard, and client-drive providers are authorized independently.
Only shadow mode is available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --mode " shadow"
Select shadow mode. Managed sessions are rejected.
.TP
.BI --source " display:index|window:id"
Select a ScreenCaptureKit display by zero-based list index or a window by its
nonzero CoreGraphics identifier. The default is
.BR display:0 .
.TP
.BI --bind " address"
Set the listener address. The default is
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Set the RDP listener port.
.TP
.BI --max-peers " count"
Limit concurrent peers.
.TP
.BI --max-fps " count"
Limit capture and frame delivery to the configured rate.
.TP
.BI --max-frame-bytes " bytes"
Limit one normalized BGRA frame to the configured byte count.
.TP
.BI --security " tls|nla|standard"
Select server security. TLS is the default.
.TP
.BI --tls-cert " path"
Load the TLS certificate from an absolute path.
.TP
.BI --tls-key " path"
Load the TLS private key from an absolute path.
.TP
.B --allow-standard-security
Permit explicitly selected Standard RDP Security.
.TP
.BI --user " name"
Set the account accepted by NLA authentication.
.TP
.BI --domain " name"
Set the optional NLA authentication domain.
.TP
.BI --password-env " name"
Read the NLA authentication secret from the named environment variable. The
default variable name is
.BR LIBRDP_SERVER_PASSWORD .
.TP
.B --allow-capture
Grant access to the selected capture source. This option is required.
.TP
.B --allow-input
Request remote keyboard and pointer injection. macOS Accessibility permission
is also required.
.TP
.B --allow-clipboard
Grant bidirectional clipboard access after local consent.
.TP
.B --allow-drive
Grant read-only access to client-announced drives after local consent.
.TP
.BI --drive-mount " path"
Select an absolute, isolated mount point for client-announced drives. An
available FUSE 3 provider is required.
.TP
.B --non-interactive
Do not request macOS privacy permissions or show application consent dialogs.
Screen Recording and Accessibility access must already be granted.
.TP
.B --help
Print command usage.
.SH PERMISSIONS
Screen Recording permission is required for capture. Accessibility permission
is required only when input is enabled. Clipboard and drive grants are
independent; denial disables the affected provider without enabling it
implicitly.
.SH SECURITY
TLS and NLA require absolute certificate and private-key paths. NLA credentials
must be supplied through the environment selected by
.BR --password-env ;
they are not accepted as command arguments. Standard RDP Security is rejected
unless
.B --allow-standard-security
is also supplied.
.SH CLIENT DRIVES
Client-announced drives are mounted read-only below the path selected by
.BR --drive-mount .
The option does not redirect macOS host files to the remote client. Mounts,
handles, and pending requests are removed when their owning peer disconnects.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Revoke capture, input, clipboard, and client-drive consent while keeping the
listener running.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop the listener and release peers and native providers.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR librdp-server (7),
.BR librdp (7)
